{"clock":1,"nonce":"d802a144945c7eaba6390309942e6206","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1794412582,"data":{"body":"Today a delete in git-board (DELETE /api/issues/{id}, a tombstone; ADR 0004 §6) leaves every forge copy open and linked: the sync never sends a delete. No page has a Delete button (web/src/api/issues.ts deleteIssue() is unused).\n\nThe user (2026-11-11, testing on a real board): \"we can close issue, but not delete them.. that would avoid having to sync deleted items to other forge\" and \"close issues and deleted issues are different things in forges already\".\n\n## Proposals (Fable 5.2, 2026-11-11)\n\n| | A git-board delete does on the forges | Size |\n|---|---|---|\n| P1 | Nothing (today), plus a Delete button | ~3 files |\n| P2 | Refused for a linked issue: close only | ~5 files |\n| P3 | Always close, with a note | ~8 files |\n| P4 (recommended) | Per forge: on_delete = \"keep\" / \"close\" / \"delete\" | ~12 files, a DeleteIssue forge method |\n| P5 | P4, plus a forge delete deletes here and on the other forges | risky: a token losing access reads as a mass delete |\n\nP4 design:\n- `on_delete` on each `[forges.\u003cname\u003e]`, beside `way` (forge/conf.go:32); empty means close; `way = \"pull\"` is always keep.\n- Trigger in the push loop where a deleted issue is skipped today (domain/issues/issuesync/sync.go:947); pull (:666) and mayCreate (:1007) unchanged.\n- close: SetStatus(closed) unless seen closed, plus one note \"Deleted in git-board by \u003clogin\u003e on \u003cdate\u003e. This issue no longer syncs.\"\n- delete: only with the deleter's own token (`r.writer` direct, sync.go:423), else close. GitHub: GraphQL deleteIssue (admin, org must allow it). GitLab: DELETE /projects/:id/issues/:iid (Planner/Owner).\n- Outcome recorded once: seen field \"deleted\" = closed / deleted / gone (sync/state.go:165-171); refusals through r.refuse (warn once).\n- forge.Forge gains DeleteIssue; fake, GitHub, GitLab adapters; conformance case beside deletionsNotPropagated (forge/forgetest/forgetest.go:557).\n- UI: Delete in the issue's menu, a confirm naming what happens on each forge; same text in the CLI confirm (surface/cli/write.go:633).\n- Docs: ADR 0004 §6, docs/spec/sync.md:494-507, data-model.md, forges.md.\n\nGaps found on the way:\n- A delete made on a forge is not detected: listings are incremental, so it just disappears; a pending local change re-reads it every run (sync.go:960-962, plan.go:769-773). Phase 2: record seen deleted = \"gone\", show \"deleted on GitHub\" with a Delete button; a person decides.\n- GitHub SetStatus sends only state (forge/github/github.go:316-318): a close's reason (not planned, duplicate) never reaches GitHub.\n- The Project bridge warns \"no matching issue\" on every run for a deleted issue's item (tools/ghproject/plan.go:433-436).\n\n## Decisions for the user\n1. Default close (recommended), or keep until a team opts in?\n2. Real delete only with the deleter's own token (recommended), or the posting account too?\n3. Send not_planned on GitHub (fixes normal closes too; a separate change)?\n4. Post the \"Deleted in git-board\" note, or close silently?\n5. Forge-side deletes: flag them, a person decides (recommended), or leave undetected?\n6. Project item: clearer warning (recommended), or remove it when write = true?","title":"Deleting an issue: what it does on the forges (keep, close or delete)"}},{"kind":"change-labels","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1794412582,"data":{"add":["kind:feat","status:backlog"],"remove":null}}]}